(6) Development as discourse: Truman 1949; Escobar and Sachs
(7) The thesis applied (1): the "Third World woman" as victim — Mohanty
(8) The thesis applied (2): outside experts, donor agendas and debt conditions
(9) The thesis applied (3): extraction through global supply chains
(10) The thesis applied (4): Western gender models imposed
(11) The counter-argument: real gains; Southern ownership; women's own demands
(12) Pakistan: IMF conditions, donor projects, supply chains — and home-grown reform
(13) Conclusion: decolonise development rather than abandon it
